# LibreWolf no-adjust.patch  (Android)
# Owner: LW-M4-02 ("Remove the Adjust install-attribution SDK")
#
# Removes the proprietary Adjust install-attribution SDK, the Google Play
# install-referrer client that feeds it, and every call site of both.
#
#
# 157 REBASE (2026-10-02, Android leaves ESR for Firefox release 157.0)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Intent unchanged: the SDK, the Play install-referrer client, every consumer
# of the referrer and every call site go; no stubs. Regenerated against a
# pristine 157.0 tree with common.txt + the android.txt entries before it
# applied. What moved or is new on 157:
#   * TWO MORE FILES DELETED, both new upstream since 153:
#       .../components/metrics/AdjustSdkController.kt -- 157's test seam
#           around Adjust's static entry points (initSdk/enable/trackEvent/
#           gdprForgetMe); its only user was AdjustMetricsService.
#       .../components/metrics/ReferralAttribution.kt (+ ReferralAttributionTest.kt)
#           -- 157's "Firefox referral code" path (bug 2062793): extracts an
#           `fxrefer<code>` utm_content from the Play install referrer and
#           submits it on the Glean `referrals` ping. Its only caller was
#           InstallReferrerWorker, so like RtamoAttributionHandler it has no
#           input left and goes rather than becoming dead code.
#           Settings.referralCode / referralPingSubmitted are LEFT, as inert
#           storage read only by the debug drawer (DistributionTools.kt) --
#           the same category as Settings.utm* below. The `referrals` ping and
#           Referrals.code metric definitions are metrics.yaml/pings.yaml,
#           i.e. LW-M4-01's, and are left too.
#   * libs.versions.toml: adjust is 5.8.0 on 157 (was 5.7.0); same four lines.
#   * Settings.kt hunk DROPPED, intent kept without it. 157 already defaults
#     shouldShowMarketingOnboarding to `false`, and the page logic inverted:
#     MarketingPageAdditionSupport / OnboardingFragment.pagesToDisplay ADD the
#     MARKETING_DATA page only while the pref is true. Its only writers were in
#     the deleted InstallReferrerHandlingService, so it stays false forever --
#     the effective behaviour the 153 one-line flip existed to preserve.
#     Nothing in main/ reads utmParamsKnown or the isUser*Attributed prefs on
#     157 either (checked), so no other default needed attention.
#   * DistributionIdManager.kt / DistributionSettings.kt: the same members are
#     removed (upstream reformatted them to 120 columns); the
#     DistributionAdjustStartupStrategy enum is now top-level-documented with
