# WHAT WAS ACTUALLY IN THE APK BEFORE THIS PATCH (measured, not grepped)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read out of ~/lw-m2-04/out-make/apk/fenix-x86_64-debug.apk (the LW-M2-04
# build, versionName 1.0.2634, buildID 20260816204534) by parsing the DEX
# class_defs / type_ids / string_ids tables of all 36 classes*.dex, and by
# `aapt2 dump xmltree --file AndroidManifest.xml` on the same APK:
#
#   * 324 Adjust strings in the dex string table -- the number
#     `./scripts/android-smoke.sh --check-no-adjust` reports (307 for the needle
#     "com/adjust/sdk", 15 for "com.adjust.sdk", 2 for "adjust_config", and 0 --
#     see the note below -- for "com.android.vending.INSTALL_REFERRER").
#   * 358 classes DEFINED in the dex (class_defs, not merely referenced),
#     counted by descriptor prefix:
#         300  Lcom/adjust/sdk/                      the SDK itself
#          12  Lcom/android/installreferrer/         the Play referrer library
#           3  Lcom/google/android/finsky/externalreferrer/
#                                                    its AIDL client, which binds
#                                                    into the Play Store
#          16  Lorg/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/InstallReferrer*
#          10  Lorg/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/Adjust*
#           8  Lorg/mozilla/fenix/...Rtamo*
#           4  Lorg/mozilla/fenix/...UTMParams* / MetaParams*
#           2  Lorg/mozilla/fenix/...ConversionEventRecorder*
#           2  ...DistributionAdjustStartupStrategy (+1 referenced-only array type)
#           1  Lorg/mozilla/fenix/...DefaultInstallReferrerClient
#   * the SDK reaches for three optional plugin modules by reflection, and the
#     class names are in the string table: com.adjust.sdk.imei.Util,
#     com.adjust.sdk.huawei.Util, com.adjust.sdk.google.lvl.Util. The first of
#     those reads the device IMEI.
#   * a PREBUILT PROPRIETARY NATIVE LIBRARY, one per ABI:
#         lib/<abi>/libsigner.so   1,274,704 bytes for x86_64, stripped
#     `file` reports "built by NDK r26c ... clang version 17.0.2", i.e. it was
#     NOT produced by this project's pinned NDK r29 toolchain and nothing in the
#     LibreWolf build can reproduce it. Its exported symbols say what it is:
#         Java_com_adjust_sdk_sig_NativeLibHelper_nSign
#         Java_com_adjust_sdk_sig_NativeLibHelper_nOnResume
#     -- Adjust's closed-source request-signing blob. Nobody had noticed it,
#     because it is not a class and no source-tree grep finds it: it rides in
#     inside the adjust-android AAR. It goes with the dependency (measured: the
#     patched APK has 15 native libraries where the baseline had 16, and
#     libsigner.so is the whole difference).
#   * in the MERGED manifest, four entities, only ONE of which is written in
#     Fenix's own AndroidManifest.xml -- the rest arrive through manifest
#     merging, which is exactly the failure mode this task was warned about:
#       <uses-permission com.adjust.preinstall.READ_PERMISSION>        (Fenix)
#       <receiver com.adjust.sdk.AdjustPreinstallReferrerReceiver>     (Fenix)
#           with <action com.attribution.SYSTEM_INSTALLER_REFERRER>
#       <provider com.adjust.sdk.SystemLifecycleContentProvider>       (Adjust AAR)
#           authorities ${applicationId}.adjust-lifecycle-provider
#       <uses-permission
#           com.google.android.finsky.permission.BIND_GET_INSTALL_REFERRER_SERVICE>
#                                                            (installreferrer AAR)
#
# NOTE for anyone reading the smoke harness: there is NO
# `com.android.vending.INSTALL_REFERRER` string in the dex of the stock build and
# no receiver carrying that action in the stock MERGED manifest -- measured, both
# before and after this patch, so that needle of --check-no-adjust scores 0 either
# way. What the version here (adjust-android 5.7.0) actually registers is the
# ContentProvider above plus the Play referrer API; whether earlier versions used
# the classic broadcast receiver is not something this task measured. Two
# consequences: the "INSTALL_REFERRER receiver" named in the acceptance is
# AdjustPreinstallReferrerReceiver (action com.attribution.SYSTEM_INSTALLER_REFERRER)
# together with the Play referrer bind permission, not a com.android.vending
# receiver; and --check-no-adjust does not, and cannot, check the manifest at all,
# so the merged-manifest half of the acceptance had to be verified with aapt2.
# It was. See "HOW THIS WAS VERIFIED".
#
#
# THE FLAG IS ALREADY OFF, AND THAT IS NOT ABSENCE
# ------------------------------------------------
# BuildConfig.ADJUST_TOKEN is null in this configuration -- twice over:
# mobile/android/fenix/app/build.gradle read `${rootDir}/.adjust_token`, which
# does not exist in a LibreWolf tree, and android.buildTypes.debug forced
# ADJUST_TOKEN to null regardless. AdjustMetricsService.start() therefore logged
# "No adjust token defined" and returned early; a captured logcat that upstream
# itself ships as test data shows exactly that line
# (python/mozperftest/mozperftest/tests/data/home_activity.txt:951).
#
# That is not the same as absence, in four measurable ways:
#
#   1. all 307 SDK classes are in the shipped dex either way, i.e. the whole
#      attack surface and the whole third-party licence footprint ship;
#   2. com.adjust.sdk.SystemLifecycleContentProvider is registered in the merged
#      manifest either way (measured), and -- platform property, documented by
#      Android and not separately measured here -- a registered ContentProvider is
#      instantiated by the system during process start, before Application.onCreate
#      returns and so before any token check of ours runs;
#   3. AdjustMetricsService.stop() called Adjust.disable() and
#      Adjust.gdprForgetMe() with no token guard at all;
#   4. `if (Config.channel.isReleased) throw IllegalStateException("No adjust
#      token defined for release build")` means the early return is a
#      *debug-only* path: the shape upstream intends for a release build is a
#      real token, and LW-M4-07 changes the channel.
#
# So the token being empty is a configuration accident, and the acceptance for
# this task is absence. Absence is what this patch delivers.
#
#
# WHY THE PLAY INSTALL-REFERRER CLIENT GOES TOO
# ---------------------------------------------
# Not a judgement call -- removing only the SDK cannot satisfy "no INSTALL_REFERRER
# receiver in the merged manifest" and "no stubs left behind":
#
#   * BIND_GET_INSTALL_REFERRER_SERVICE and IGetInstallReferrerService come from
#     com.android.installreferrer, not from Adjust. Dropping only Adjust leaves
#     the app declaring a permission to bind the Play Store's referrer service
#     and shipping the AIDL stub for it.
#   * every consumer of the referrer response was Adjust:
#       - Settings.isUser{Meta,TikTok,Reddit,XTwitter}Attributed were written by
#         InstallReferrerWorker/InstallReferrerHandlingService and read ONLY by
#         AdjustMetricsService.applyThirdPartySharingSettings, which turned them
#         into Adjust.trackThirdPartySharing() calls for Meta, TikTok, Reddit,
#         X and Google partner IDs;
#       - InstallReferrerHandlingService.start() called
#         distributionIdManager.startAdjustIfSkippingConsentScreen(), whose body
#         is setMarketingTelemetryPreferences() + metricController.start(Marketing);
#         with the Marketing service gone that is a stub that silently enables
#         marketing telemetry;
#       - PlayStoreAttribution / MetaAttribution Glean metrics and the
#         play-store-attribution and adjust-attribution pings had no other source.
#
#
