# UTMParams: KEPT AS FIVE NAMES, NOT AS A CLASS
# ---------------------------------------------
# UTMParams lived in InstallReferrerWorker.kt. Its parser and its Glean
# recorder had no caller left, but five of its companion constants did:
# CustomAttributeProvider publishes utm_source/utm_medium/utm_campaign/
# utm_content/utm_term as Nimbus targeting attributes, and
# mobile/android/fenix/app/messaging-fenix.fml.yaml:37-38 keys its FUNNEL_PAID /
# FUNNEL_ORGANIC targeting on `adjust_campaign`, which the same object publishes.
# Deleting the names would break the FML at build time; keeping the class would
# leave a parser nothing calls. So the names become file-private constants in
# CustomAttributeProvider and the class goes.
#
# Settings.utm{Source,Medium,Campaign,Term,Content} are deliberately LEFT in
# place. Nothing writes them any more, so they read "" forever, and they are
# still read by RecordedNimbusContext, CustomAttributeProvider and the debug
# drawer. They are inert storage, not a stub; deleting the properties would pull
# in preference_keys.xml and RecordedNimbusContext for no behavioural gain.
#
#
# ONE BEHAVIOURAL REGRESSION THIS PATCH HAD TO FIX
# ------------------------------------------------
# Settings.shouldShowMarketingOnboarding defaulted to `true`, and
# InstallReferrerHandlingService was its ONLY writer: every one of its failure
# paths (FEATURE_NOT_SUPPORTED / SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE / DEVELOPER_ERROR /
# PERMISSION_ERROR / disconnect) set it to false, which is what happens on any
# device without a Play Store answering the referrer bind -- i.e. on every
# device LibreWolf targets. Deleting the writer and leaving the default at
# `true` would have turned the MARKETING_DATA onboarding page ON for the first
# time, because MarketingPageRemovalSupport only ever *removes* that page and
# only when the pref is false. So the default flips to `false` in the same
# change. That is the previous *effective* behaviour, not a new decision, and
# it is one line in Settings.kt.
#
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT TOUCHED (and why), so a checked absence and an overlooked
# one do not look the same
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   * mobile/android/android-components/build.gradle:53
#       `exclude group: 'com.adjust.sdk', module: 'adjust-android'` stays. It is
#       a guard against a-c pulling Adjust back in transitively, and it keeps
#       working after the version-catalog entry is gone. Removing it would only
#       remove a defence.
#   * Glean definitions -- app/metrics.yaml (AdjustAttribution.*,
#     PlayStoreAttribution.*, MetaAttribution.*, Metrics.adjust*),
#     app/pings.yaml (adjust-attribution, play-store-attribution),
#     app/tags.yaml. These generate an API that now has no caller; the ping is
#     never submitted because nothing calls submit() any more. metrics.yaml is
#     LW-M4-01's file and removing metric definitions from under it would
#     collide. Flagged for LW-M4-01.
#   * FenixApplication.kt:911-914 still copies Settings.adjustCampaignId /
#     adjustNetwork / adjustAdGroup / adjustCreative into Glean's Metrics.adjust*.
#     Those four prefs now have no writer, so it copies four empty strings.
#     Same reason as above: the fix is deleting the Glean metrics, LW-M4-01.
#   * DefaultDistributionProviderChecker (distributions/DistributionProviderChecker.kt)
#       queries content providers advertising com.attribution.REFERRAL_PROVIDER
#       and reads an `encrypted_data` column. That is the OEM/carrier preinstall
#       partner protocol, not the Adjust SDK, and it feeds only the distribution
#       ID. It stays, but note that this patch removes the
#       com.adjust.preinstall.READ_PERMISSION that let it read a protected
#       provider, so on a partner preload the query now returns null and the
#       distribution degrades to Distribution.DEFAULT -- which is what LibreWolf
#       wants, since LibreWolf has no distribution deals. Whether the whole
#       distribution mechanism should go is LW-M4-07's call, not this patch's.
#   * Event.GrowthData / Event.FirstWeekPostInstall (components/metrics/Event.kt)
#       carry the Adjust event tokens ("xgpcgt", "41hl22", ...). After this patch
#       no MetricsService accepts those events, so GrowthDataWorker and
#       MetricsMiddleware track into nothing. Event is still Fenix's generic
#       event model and GleanMetricsService still tracks Events with a wrapper,
#       so this is Fenix telemetry plumbing, not Adjust: LW-M4-01's territory.
#   * python/mozperftest/.../home_activity.txt is a frozen logcat capture used as
#       python test data. Not code, and not in mobile/.
#   * Settings.rtamoAddonDownloadUrl / rtamoAddonName / rtamoAddonImageUrl and the
#       `if (downloadUrl.isNotBlank())` branch in OnboardingFragment.onFinish that
#       reads them. RtamoAttributionHandler was the only writer, so the branch is
#       now unreachable and the three prefs read "" forever -- the same inert-storage
#       category as Settings.utm* and Settings.adjust* above, and OnboardingFragment
#       is LW-M4-10's file. Measured in the built APK: the 10 RtamoAttributionHandler
#       classes are gone and the only "rtamo" classes left are two Glean-generated
#       ones, GleanMetrics/Addons$RtamoFailedExtra and $RtamoIdentifiedExtra, which
#       come from metrics.yaml (LW-M4-01).
#
